 fuse [linux-any] | fuse4bsd [kfreebsd-any]
Description: mergerfs fork with indexed read-only branches
 lazyfs is a fork of mergerfs, a union filesystem geared towards simplifying storage and
 management of files across numerous commodity storage devices. It is
 similar to mhddfs, unionfs, and aufs. It adds ROC branches whose
 metadata is served from an index so sleeping drives stay asleep,
 and can read cloud mirrors of their files. It installs alongside
 mergerfs.
